hadiths[10]{hadithnumber,text}:
"15501","Abd al-Razzaq and Rawh both said: Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, he said: Hasan ibn Muslim informed me, from Tawus, from a man who had met the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Tawaf is but a prayer, so when you perform tawaf, speak little. And Muhammad ibn Bakr did not raise it to the Prophet."
"15981","Waki' narrated to us, he said, Shu'ba narrated to us, from Amr ibn Murra, from Murra al-Tayyib, he said, a man of the Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) narrated to me in this room of mine, I think he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) addressed us on the Day of Sacrifice upon a red she-camel of his, and said: This is the Day of Sacrifice, and this is the day of the Greater Hajj."
"20873","Ibn Abi Adi narrated to us, from Sulayman, meaning al-Taymi, from Anas, from one of the Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: On the night I was taken, I passed by Musa, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, while he was praying in his grave."
"20876","Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Khalid, from Abu Qilabah, from Muhammad ibn Abi Aishah, from a man among the Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Perhaps you recite behind the imam while the imam is reciting. They said: We do that. He said: So do not do it, except that one of you recite the Mother of the Book, or he said: The Opening of the Book."
"20927","Yahya ibn Said al-Umawi narrated to us from Asim who said: Abu al-Aliyah narrated to us, he said: One who heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, informed me, he said: Every surah has its share of bowing and prostration. He said: Then I met him after and said to him: Ibn Umar used to recite several surahs in one rakah, so do you know who narrated this hadith to you. He said: I know him and know since when he narrated it to me: He narrated it to me fifty years ago."
"20928","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us from Ubaydullah, Nafi narrated to me, he said: Sometimes Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both, would lead us reciting two and three surahs."
"20944","Affan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, Said al-Jurayri informed us from Abu Nadrah who said: A man from the companions of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, fell ill, and his companions entered upon him visiting him, and he wept. It was said to him: What makes you weep, O Abdullah, did the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, not say to you: Take from your mustache then keep it until you meet me. He said: Yes, but I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: Allah, blessed and exalted, took a handful with His right hand and said: These for these, and I do not care, and another handful, meaning with His other hand, and said: These for these, and I do not care. So I do not know in which of the two handfuls I am."
"20959","Ali ibn Asim narrated to us, Sulayman al-Taymi informed us, he said: Al-Hasan narrated to me with the hadith of Abu Uthman al-Nahdi from Umar about silk. He said: Al-Hasan said: A man of the tribe informed me that he entered upon the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, wearing a cloak whose opening was silk. He said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: A patch of fire."
"20967","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us from Khalid al-Hadhdha from Abu Qilabah from one who heard the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, recite: So that Day none punishes as His punishment, and none binds as His binding, meaning He does to him. Khalid said: I asked Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Bakrah, he said: So that Day none punishes, meaning He does to him."
"20968","Affan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, al-Azraq ibn Qays narrated to us from Yahya ibn Yamur from a man from the companions of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, who said: The first of what the servant will be judged by on the Day of Resurrection is his prayer. If he completed it, it will be written for him complete, and if he did not complete it, He says: See if you find for My servant voluntary acts, then complete what he wasted of his obligation. Then zakah, then deeds will be taken accordingly."
